    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 36 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (36 passed). I couldn't measure coverage, since only the test command was allowed, so the 90% gate is unverified. By reading the code, every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by a test, so I expect it to pass. The implementation validates items first, then checks coupon validity (expiry inclusive, used codes, minimum subtotal, kind), then computes the discount (percent capped by the 0–100 range, fixed capped at the subtotal). Shipping is decided on the discounted subtotal, with no shipping for an empty item list. The final total is quantized to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Two of my first test expectations were wrong (a 10% coupon on 100.00 leaves 90.00, which triggers shipping, so the total is 100.00); I corrected the tests, not the implementation.",
